l mention no cleanup needed implicitly by not polluting.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider whether to use LooseVersion at all. Risk: the module might have been changed. Let me just call get_info on the relevant names and adapt.\n\nQueries (batch, independent):\n- `Version`\n- `LooseVersion`\n- `Version.parse`\n- `Version._cmp`\n- `LooseVersion.parse`\n- `LooseVersion._cmp`\n- `LooseVersion.__str__`\n- `LooseVersion.__init__`\n\nThat's 8 calls; maybe trim to essentials: `Version`, `LooseVersion`, `Version.parse`, `LooseVersion._cmp`, `LooseVersion.parse`, `LooseVersion.__str__`. I'll do a reasonable set.\n\nAfter getting info, write the final test script.\n\nLet me draft the final test file now (to be adjusted after tool results):\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for ansible.module_utils.compat.version.Version plumbing.\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ansible.module_utils.compat.version import LooseVersion, Version\n\n\nclass DummyVersion(Version):\n    \"\"\"Minimal concrete Version used to exercise the abstract base class.\n\n    Deliberately does *not* override ``__init__`` so that ``Version.__init__``\n    itself runs, and returns ``NotImplemented`` from ``_cmp`` for unsupported\n    operand types so the base-class rich comparators propagate it.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def parse(self, vstring):\n        self.version = tuple(int(part) for part in vstring.split(\".\"))\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \".\".join(str(part) for part in self.version)\n\n    def _cmp(self, other):\n        if isinstance(other, str):\n            other = DummyVersion(other)\n        if not isinstance(other, DummyVersion):\n            return NotImplemented\n        if self.version == other.version:\n            return 0\n        if self.version < other.version:\n            return -1\n        return 1\n\n\ndef test_version_init_parses_vstring():\n    v = DummyVersion(\"1.2.3\")\n    assert v.version == (1, 2, 3)\n\n\ndef test_version_init_without_vstring_skips_parse():\n    v = DummyVersion()